<h2>Saving Forms</h2>

<p>
    When you're done editing a form:
</p>

<ol>
    <li>Click the <strong>"Save"</strong> button</li>
    <li>Quickfire creates a new version with your changes</li>
    <li>The form is saved and ready to use</li>
</ol>

<p>
    <strong>Important:</strong> Each save creates a new version. If you make multiple small changes, you might want to save once at the end rather than after every single field edit. However, saving frequently is safe—you can always revert if needed.
</p>

<p>
    After saving, you can:
</p>

<ul>
    <li>Attach the form to a client or renewal</li>
    <li>Download it as a PDF</li>
    <li>Send it via email</li>
    <li>Use it in a proposal</li>
    <li>Continue editing later</li>
</ul>

