<h2>Certificate Editor</h2>

<p>
    The Certificate Editor is a specialized form editor for creating certificates of insurance. It has special features that make certificate creation faster and easier.
</p>

<h3>Policy Dropdown Auto-Fill</h3>

<p>
    The certificate editor includes a policy dropdown that automatically fills in certificate information when you select a policy:
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Insured name</strong> – Automatically filled from the policy</li>
    <li><strong>Coverage details</strong> – Policy types and coverages are populated</li>
    <li><strong>Policy numbers</strong> – Filled in automatically</li>
    <li><strong>Effective and expiration dates</strong> – Copied from the policy</li>
    <li><strong>Carrier information</strong> – Insurance company details are added</li>
</ul>

<p>
    <strong>How to use it:</strong>
</p>

<ol>
    <li>Open the certificate editor</li>
    <li>Click the <strong>"Policies"</strong> button or dropdown</li>
    <li>Select one or more policies from the list</li>
    <li>Click <strong>"Update"</strong> to fill in the certificate</li>
    <li>Review and adjust any fields that need changes</li>
    <li>Save the certificate</li>
</ol>

<p>
    This saves significant time compared to typing everything manually, and it reduces errors by pulling information directly from your policy records.
</p>

